* Power-law curves
** Definition
*** y = a * x^k
*** k sets the shape, a the scale
*** k < 0, 0 < k < 1, k = 1, k > 1
** Scale invariance
*** f(cx) = c^k * f(x)
*** Constant elasticity = k
*** Doubling x multiplies y by 2^k
** Log-log plot
*** Straight line of slope k
*** k from two points
** Versus other curves
*** Linear: special case k = 1
*** Exponential overtakes any power
left side
** Calculus
*** Integral of x^k is x^(k+1)/(k+1)
*** k = -1 gives a logarithm
** In DeFi and finance
*** Bonding curves: p = alpha * s^beta
*** Constant product: y = K / x
*** Weighted pools: y ~ x^(-w1/w2)
*** Square-root price impact (empirical)
** Distributions
*** Pareto tail P(X > x) ~ x^(-alpha)
*** 80/20 rule: alpha ~ 1.16
*** Fit by maximum likelihood, not by a log-log line
